LightCraft is an open-source, clean-room photo library and raw
developer in the style of Adobe Lightroom, written in Rust.  It
offers non-destructive editing through a scene-referred, wide-gamut
32-bit float pipeline, colour grading, brush/gradient/range masks,
presets and profiles, and a library with albums, folders, ratings and
flags.  Raw decoders for DNG, CR2, ARW, NEF, RAF (incl. X-Trans), RW2,
PEF and ORF are included.  Every action is a command that can also be
driven from lightcraft-cli or an MCP server.
